#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:2
msgid "Disk space awareness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:4
msgid ""
"The snap daemon, _snapd_, can check whether there is enough free disk space "
"before performing the following space-requiring operations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:6
msgid "**snap installation**: checks storage required to download a snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:7
msgid ""
"**snap refresh and update**: checks storage required to download updates and "
"to store previous snap revisions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:8
msgid ""
"**snap removal**: checks storage required to create the {ref}`automatic "
"snapshot <ref-create-data-snapshots_automatic-snapshots>` generated when the "
"last revision of a snap is removed (unless disabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:11
msgid "Disk space awareness is currently an experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:14
msgid ""
"When enabled, snapd checks whether there is enough space in `/var/lib/snapd` "
"to complete an operation, such as enough space to store a requested snap to "
"download. If there isn't enough space, an error is returned and the "
"operation is not performed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:16
msgid ""
"$ snap install foo\n"
"error: cannot install \"foo\" due to low disk space\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:21
msgid ""
"The error output can also include a hint on how a space requirement could be "
"mitigated, such as suggesting the `--purge` flag with `snap remove` to "
"disable the automatic snapshot generation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:23
msgid ""
"$ snap remove foo\n"
"error: cannot remove \"foo\" due to low disk space, use --purge to avoid "
"creating a snapshot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:28
msgid ""
"The {ref}`REST API <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-use-the-rest-api>` will also "
"return an `insufficient-disk-space` {ref}`error response <reference-"
"development-rest-api-error-responses>` object when disk space awareness is "
"enabled and an error is encountered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:30
msgid "Enable disk space awareness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:32
msgid ""
"To enable disk space awareness, set one or more of the following "
"_experimental_ feature flags to _true_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:34
msgid "`experimental.check-disk-space-install`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:35
msgid "`experimental.check-disk-space-refresh`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:36
msgid "`experimental.check-disk-space-remove`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:38
msgid ""
"To enable the pre-install check, for example, use the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:39
msgid "snap set system experimental.check-disk-space-install=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/disk-space-awareness.md:43
msgid ""
"See {ref}`System options <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-set-system-options>` "
"for more details on setting and disabling options."
msgstr ""
